      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Warband" id="1771-6b1b-d3f7-bdbc" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="7baf-e3cc-f08d-8ec7" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
        <constraint id="a574-cbb4-c899-c3c4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Warband Origins" id="cac3-8971-8cd4-2595" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="fdcd-3aad-607f-599d" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Emperor&apos;s Children" id="9bda-7c1f-0f29-2044" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink name="Feel No Pain" id="9a97-449c-8e26-6d93" hidden="false" targetId="f3a2-c2b0-6b0e-1653" type="rule"/>
                <infoLink name="Fearless" id="e42a-2b1f-5bec-7c5e" hidden="false" targetId="8220-efb5-2199-6d3d" type="rule"/>
              </infoLinks>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Emperor&apos;s Children" id="5901-6e44-6d4d-2ff2" hidden="false">
                  <description>An Emperor’s Children Detachment retains the Chaos Space Marines Faction and is treated in all ways as a Chaos Space Marines Detachment, with the following modifications:

Positives: 
•	Chosen and Noise Marines with Veterans of the Long War may be taken as a Troops choice.
•	Psykers from the Detachment can choose to generate all of their psychic powers from the Discipline of Slaanesh.

Negatives: 
•	They cannot include any Unique units other than Lucius the Eternal, Fulgrim and Lord Commander Eidelon. 
•	Units that can take the Mark of Slaanesh must do so.
•	Units with a Mark of Chaos other than the Mark of Slaanesh cannot be taken.
•	Any Daemon Princes must have the Daemon of Slaanesh special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Fueled by Sensation" id="d204-ba48-6b3f-1810" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units that have the Veterans of the Long War special rule have the Fearless and Feel No Pain (6+) special rules (units with an Icon of Excess instead have the Fearless and Feel No Pain (4+) special rules).

In addition, if a model that has the Veterans of the Long War special rule is slain in the Fight sub-phase before it has made any Attacks that phase, it can make a single Attack at the end of the current Initiative step before being removed as a casualty.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Slaves to Excess" id="4473-3dec-728f-d22f" hidden="false">
                  <description>Emperor’s Children characters must always issue/accept challenges when possible (Although which characters fight the challenge is up to them). However, if they are defeated in combat and their challenger is slain, all Emperor&apos;s Children units in the army suffer a -1 penalty to their leadership for the remainder of the turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="World Eaters" id="99a1-e39c-fca4-2552" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="World Eaters" id="a674-ab87-0709-1efe" hidden="false">
                  <description>A World Eaters Detachment retains the Chaos Space Marines Faction and is treated in all ways as a Chaos Space Marines Detachment, with the following modifications:

Positives: 
•	Chosen and Khorne Berserker&apos;s with the Veterans of the Long War special rule may be taken as a Troops choice.
•       Units that have the Veterans of the Long War special rule have the Fearless and Furious Charge special rules.

Negatives: 
•	They cannot include any Unique characters other than Kharne the Betrayer and Daemon Primarch Angron.
•	Units that can take the Mark of Khorne must do so.
•	Units with a Mark of Chaos other than the Mark of Khorne cannot be taken.
•	Any Daemon Princes must have the Daemon of Khorne special rule.
•       They cannot include Psykers.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="The Butcher&apos;s Nails" id="d5f5-4842-865a-2612" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units with this special rule must always make Sweeping Advances if able, but cannot voluntarily Go to Ground or fail a Morale check. They must always Consolidate towards the nearest enemy unit they are able to harm.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="The Blessing of Khorne" id="ba18-72fc-1e99-e4cd" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units that have the Veterans of the Long War special rule have the Adamantium Will, Furious Charge and Fearless special rules.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Word Bearers" id="c325-7487-bdcf-0075" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Alpha Legion" id="e793-4cfb-238d-1995" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Night Lords" id="2f36-40f1-98b2-a269" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink name="Fear" id="68ab-cfd5-b816-e0a8" hidden="false" targetId="bbca-34a4-2d3d-8d2a" type="rule"/>
              </infoLinks>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Night Lords" id="ad9b-9c9d-6a7a-dbac" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Night Lords Detachment retains the Chaos Space Marines Faction and is treated in all ways as a Chaos Space Marines Detachment, with the following modifications:

Positives: 
•	Terror Squads may be taken as Troops choices.
•       Night Lords units may take weapons from the Armoury of the Night Lords
•       Night Lords characters may use Night Lords Warlord Traits. 
•       Night Lords Dream Eaters may use the Nostramun Psychic Discipline

Negatives: 
•	They cannot include any Unique units other than Decimus Prophet of the 8th Legion, Terror Squads, Night Raptors and Contekar Terminators
•	Units that have a Mark of Chaos cannot be taken nor can a unit be upgraded to take any Mark of Chaos.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="In Midnight Clad" id="4dee-3231-f4ec-414d" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units that have the Veterans of the Long War special rule have Fear (1). Units with an Icon of Despair instead have the Fear (2) special rule and have a +1 modifier to wounds made against units that are Pinned or Falling Back. units that are apart of a Night Lords detachment have the Night Vision special rule, but must reduce To Hit rolls by -1 in both the shooting and fight phases against any Unit which ignores Night Fighting rules.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Nostraman Blood" id="38fc-5fa9-138f-68c3" hidden="false">
                  <description>All models with this rule Fall Back +2” more than usual. If they fail a Pinning test, they may fall back instead of being pinned. If the army’s Warlord is slain, then every model with this rule must take an immediate Morale Check and if the Warlord was a unique character they must instead take an immediate Morale check with a minus 1 to their leadership.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Iron Warriors" id="b8d9-4c2f-912d-fe49" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink name="Hatred" id="d864-9afb-8aae-d0a6" hidden="false" targetId="a6b0-c95c-c78f-b0ab" type="rule"/>
                <infoLink name="Feel No Pain" id="c2b7-a516-a56b-68db" hidden="false" targetId="f3a2-c2b0-6b0e-1653" type="rule"/>
              </infoLinks>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Iron Warriors" id="d38e-6428-10ce-d6f8" hidden="false">
                  <description>An Iron Warriors Detachment retains the Chaos Space Marines Faction and is treated in all ways as a Chaos Space Marines Detachment, with the following modifications:

Positives: 
•       Iron Warriors units may take weapons from the Armoury of the Iron Warriors
•       Iron Warriors characters may use Iron Warriors Warlord Traits. 
•       Iron Warriors gain the Iron Within, Iron Without and Siege Masters special rules. 


Negatives: 
•	They cannot include any Unique units other than Honsou, Tyrant Siege Terminators, Warsmiths and the Primarch Perturabo. 
•	Units that have a Mark of Chaos cannot be taken nor can a unit be upgraded to take any Mark of Chaos. 
•	Iron Warrior&apos;s units may not take any Icon&apos;s of Chaos, with the exception of the Icon of Vengeance. 
•	Iron Warrior&apos;s detachment have the &quot;Abhore the Mutant, Abhore the Psyker&quot; special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Abhore the Mutant, Abhore the Psyker" id="6408-4780-efdd-e566" hidden="false">
                  <description>An Iron Warriors detachment may take only one of the following: Chaos Spawn, Obliterators, Mutilators. In addition, An Iron Warrior&apos;s model may never become a psyker and sorcerer&apos;s cannot be taken by an Iron Warriors Warband. Note this does not effect Daemon sorcerer&apos;s in an Iron Warrior&apos;s army.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Iron Within, Iron Without" id="c4e7-8561-0de7-6ec3" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units in an Iron Warrior&apos;s detachment gain (Hatred) Imperial Fists. In addition, units with the Veteran&apos;s of the Long War rule gain the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Siege Masters" id="4f1b-1777-cfd1-a52b" hidden="false">
                  <description>When a model with this special rule makes a Shooting Attack or Melee Attack targeting a model with the Dreadnought, Automata, Vehicle or Building Unit Type, it gains +1 to the Strength of that attack.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
    </selectionEntry>
