    <selectionEntry name="Formations" id="e4c8-6c39-df74-8ecb" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="60c2-bbc5-3eb1-6c31" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Warband Specific Formations" id="6e0b-41d8-f713-aa03" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="fa69-7b45-edc8-6a97" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="The Red Tide" id="19a1-13e0-5eb1-fe00" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="The Red Tide" id="b498-6d81-b784-c276" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Red tide is a World Eaters specific Formation which confers the following rules.

Khorne Berserkers must be taken as compulsory units. 
If you choose to take Terminators, they may only be Red Butchers. 
Your Warlord must be a Chaos Lord with the Mark of Khorne, Kharne the Betrayer or The Daemon Primarch Angron. 
In additon you recieve the following abilities:

Lost to Rage: Units with the Mark of Khorne must always attempt to charge the closest enemy unit within 12&quot; and add +1 to their charges. They must always make sweeping advances and consolidate towards the nearest enemy unit. In addition, they recieve the benefit of a 6+ Feel No Pain. 

Ravening Madmen: Enemies always hit all units with a Mark of Khorne on a 3+ regardless of weapon skill. These units can never be scoring units.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="The Kakophoni" id="feef-6e22-79fb-d394" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="The Kakophoni" id="78dd-054d-2a51-f853" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Kakophoni is a Emperor&apos;s Children formation which confers the following rules: 

Noise Marines must be taken as compulsory troops choice and gain the relentless special rule. 
An Emperor&apos;s Children force which takes this formation cannot be accompanied by any Allied force except Daemons of Slaanesh. 

Lost to the Sound
If two Noise Marine Squads (totalling at least 10 models) are within coherency with each other, then, in the shooting phase, these units gain +1 to the Strength of their Sonic Blasters. Whilst these units are in coherency, they may not act as scoring units for the purpose of any mission.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Pride of the Warband" id="d710-0246-13ea-f7b3" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="e8b2-12b0-b89f-9535" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Pride of the Warband" id="052d-882d-b1ff-2b8e" hidden="false">
                  <description>Chosen squads and Terminator squads are Troops choices in the force, and units of either of these types must be selected as the force’s compulsory Troops choices. This also includes any Warband specific Terminator squads. 


Should all Chosen squads and Terminator squads in the force be destroyed in the battle, then the enemy counts as having scored an additional Secondary Objective worth 2 Victory points.
• You may not take an Allied Force Detachment.
• The majority of the units in the detachment must not have the Daemon, Daemonic Possession or Daemonforge special rules.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="The Murder Talon" id="d6a5-bc44-6705-0951" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="49be-0c4a-7333-b4ea" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink name="Fleet" id="c9f0-ae55-fd4b-8d98" hidden="false" targetId="b1ba-0709-4305-88e2" type="rule"/>
              </infoLinks>
              <rules>
                <rule name="The Murder Talon" id="78ad-713c-ab7e-7367" hidden="false">
                  <description>• Night Fighting rules are always in effect at the start of the first Game Turn of the battle and remain in play until the end of the second Game Turn. At the start of the third Game Turn, before any Reserves rolls are made or any models are moved, the controlling player of a Detachment using this formation may have the Night Fighting rules automatically end, or may roll a D6. If the result of the roll is a ‘4’ or greater, then the Night Fighting rules remain in effect for the duration of the third Game Turn. If the result of the roll is a ‘3’ or less, then the Night Fighting rules end immediately. At the start of the fourth turn the Night Fighting rules are automatically removed from play, regardless of the effect of any other special rule.
• Night Raptor Squads may be taken as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Formation
• Whilst Night Fighting is in effect, all Night Lords models gain Fleet (1)

Limitations
• This formation may only be selected for a Primary Detachment.
• Detachments taking this formation must take 3 compulsory troops choices and these must be either Terror Squads or Night Raptor Squads
• Detachments using this formation  may only take a single Heavy Support choice as part of their Force Organisation chart.
• An army whose Primary Detachment has this Formation may not include any Lords of War choices or models with the Super-heavy Sub-type.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
    </selectionEntry>
