              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="2ba2-3a82-dfb7-7849">Primarch (Unique)</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="M" typeId="e8fa-a6b3-0e8c-18aa">8&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="9660-0df5-9c5d-3604">8</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="565d-bf36-9e7e-29b5">6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="23ae-6026-aebd-abc3">6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="f6db-a6a5-71d2-71c5">6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="a763-cbc8-2080-a4fb">6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="ea41-893b-3f82-5482">8</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="d535-b745-b613-a7ab">6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="3b5e-ab67-ed36-a88f">10</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="d33e-1fdc-0c00-8cb8">2+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="3df9-f556-8725-fe75">Sublime Swordsman, Tactical Excellence, The Gilded Panoply,</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Warlord: Seeker of Redemption" id="f77f-2692-cdea-3abb" hidden="false">
              <description>If chosen as the army&apos;s Warlord, Fulgrim automatically has the Seeker of Redemption Warlord Trait and may not select any other Warlord Trait: 

Seeker of Redemption - All friendly models with the Warband: (Emperor’s Children) rule that can draw a line of sight to Fulgrim and do not also have the Daemon unit type may use Fulgrim’s Leadership Characteristic for all Morale and Pinning checks they are required to take and all friendly units with the Legiones Astartes (Emperor’s Children) special rule on the battlefield while Fulgrim is also on the battlefield gain +1 to the Wound value used to calculate if the unit has won a close combat. In addition, Fulgrim and any unit he joins with the Warband: Emperor&apos;s Children special rule, lose this trait&apos;s affects as well as the effects from any Marks of Chaos or Icons of Excess and instead gain Flawless Execution and In Search of Redemption

Flawless Execution: On a Turn in which they make a successful Charge, even if that Charge is considered a Disordered Charge, models with this special rule make their attacks in an assult at on initiative step higher than normal - after any initiative modifiers from other special rules have been taken into account.

In Search of Redemption: Models with this rule have +1ld and Hatred (Chaos Space Marines &amp; Daemons of Slaanesh).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
